---
# The OIDC provider's RSA signing key, from the SOPS key authelia_oidc_rsa_key_content. The
# Deployment mounts this Secret read-only at /oidc-jwk, and `jwks[].key` in
# config-secret.yaml.j2 reads /oidc-jwk/key.pem through Authelia's `template` config filter.
#
# A Secret of its own because the value is a multi-line PEM block: Flux strips every newline
# from a substituted value, so no `${...}` placeholder can carry it, and D3 ships this Secret
# as a SOPS-encrypted manifest instead (target slice R2, PR 7). `render_sops_manifests` in
# defaults/main.yml names this file, so a placeholder render leaves it out. The role's include
# lists it in `manifests_secret_files` behind authelia_k8s_manage_oidc, the lever that gates
# the `jwks` block, because authelia passes explicit lists and a template no list names never
# renders. `to_json` writes the stored key as one double-quoted scalar, newlines escaped.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: authelia-oidc-jwk
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
type: Opaque
stringData:
  key.pem: {{ authelia_oidc_rsa_key_content | to_json }}
